# Local-only working trails — NEVER push to the repo.
# Dated audit/review directories document the status of changes,
# cross-project context, session JSON dumps, etc. They are strictly local
# working artifacts. Explicit entries cover the two committed-in-error
# precedents; the date-prefix patterns prevent future recurrences.
audit_2026-05-13_waggle_session/
review_2026-05-18_v041_status/
audit_2*-*-*_*/
review_2*-*-*_*/

# Private notes and crash/debugging handoff dumps — strictly local, NEVER
# ship. notes/ holds confidential meeting/IP/legal material; *-handoff-*
# dirs are raw transcript dossiers. Both previously leaked into the sdist.
notes/
*-handoff-*/

# Cloud-sync/Finder conflict copies ("Foo 2.py", "uv 2.lock") — stale clones a
# sync tool mints beside the original. Patterns stay NARROW (the observed
# families, plus the two concrete root artifacts that were once committed)
# because broad shape-only ignores would also hide legitimately numbered files
# and directories from git status. The durable guard is sibling-based and
# tracked-file-level: tests/test_installation_health.py::TestNoSyncConflictArtifacts.
* 2.py
* 2.md
* 2.json
* [0-9].pth
pyproject [0-9]*.toml
uv [0-9]*.lock
